{"name":"Lost Love","hex":"#e5d7d4","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lost","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of lose"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having wandered from, or unable to find, the way.","In an unknown location; unable to be found."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lost"},{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lost Love (2022 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Lost Love is a 2022 Hong Kong drama film directed by Ka Sing-fung. The film stars Sammi Cheng, Alan Luk, and Hedwig Tam, and centers on a foster family navigating love, loss, and emotional healing. It premiered on 13 November 2022 at the Hong Kong Asian Film Festival as a closing film, and was theatrically released on 2 March 2023."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c0/Lost_Love_%282022_Hong_Kong_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lost_Love_(2022_film)","wikidata":"Q116116966"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love","wikidata":"Q316"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Lost_Love_%282022_Hong_Kong_film%29.jpg/250px-Lost_Love_%282022_Hong_Kong_film%29.j